Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 07:50:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06856/11362] [outer-loop] ARC su15 round-3: L7->L8,
 split-delivery race cracks the merge wall

Round-3 codex gpt-5.6-sol attempt on su15 solved L8: a split-delivery race
-- merge the two b blocks into the first c, kite it up the extreme left
edge while the two hunters fuse and the 8 processes into the second c,
then route the second c along the top edge to the far-right 9 socket.
Avoids round-2's simultaneous-control hazard (clicking near both c pieces
re-merges them into an 8) by routing along opposite edges instead of
through the center.

Source agent's own reproduction_verified is correctly false (ran out of
budget for the full 145-action reproduce() gate, though it did replay the
winning continuation successfully in a separate fresh environment).
Independently verified by the outer loop regardless: 5x fresh
env.reset() + replay via a new resolver priority branch (dict-normalized
labels), all 5 trials confirmed level=8, state=GameState.NOT_FINISHED.

L9 explored but not won: ACTION7 is a true one-step undo, an unsatisfied
d-shaped hunter-fusion requirement, and a final-level reset performs a
FULL-GAME reset (not a current-level restart). Frontier stays at level 8.

reproducible_total_levels 145 -> 146. arc_count_integrity_lint.py exit 0.

